From: RDK Build Compatibility
Subject: [PATCH] bash: include signal list after system signal headers

When NSIG is unavailable, trap.h can include signal declarations after
siglist.h defines the fallback strsignal macro. Include siglist.h last to
avoid rewriting declarations from the system headers.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/siglist.c
+++ b/siglist.c
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@
-#include "siglist.h"
-
 #if !defined (NSIG)
 #  include "trap.h"
 #endif
 
 #include "xmalloc.h"
+
+#include "siglist.h"
